Example: a price increase in a selected interval needs no new contribution.
One FUND unit was bought on 2024-01-01 at 100 USD and closed at 100 USD.
The report starts on 2024-01-02, so the previous close becomes opening value 100.
The unit closes at 120 USD on 2024-01-02 and no postings occur in the interval.
Net contributions are 0, profit/loss is 120 - 100 - 0 = 20 USD, and the
time-weighted return is 120 / 100 - 1 = 20%.
The money-weighted returns cannot be calculated for this one-day interval, so
the text formatter shows their null API values as n/a.

========== API ==========

investmentPerformance({ accounts: ['Assets:Fund'], commodities: ['FUND'], from: '2024-01-02', to: '2024-01-02' })

========== API FORMAT ==========

text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:Cash
P 2024-01-01 FUND 100 USD
P 2024-01-02 FUND 120 USD

2024-01-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2024-01-02 to 2024-01-02
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 100.00 USD
Net contributions: 0.00 USD
Ending value: 120.00 USD
Profit/loss: 20.00 USD
Time-weighted return: 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): n/a
Money-weighted return (annualized): n/a

========== WARNINGS ==========
